(* Variant quic-nocert-none: a QUIC client that got no certificate of the server (no
   QUIC_CONNECTION_EVENT_PEER_CERTIFICATE_RECEIVED), against an attacker that is the network (AUD-6, #409; CORE-H5,
   #408). Each side runs the session bound or encrypted from what its own transport gives it (TransportNoiseStart): this
   client checked no pin, so QuicStreamBinding gives it no binding, even with the exporter of its connection, and it
   runs an encrypted session with the prologue of no binding, while the server runs one bound to its exporter. The two
   prologues differ, so the handshake cannot complete, which reach-took and reach-done must prove. The model has the
   handshake of such a client, not the records under the Noise keys that it would send after one. *)

process
  ( Setup()
  | Sessions(pin_off, bt_none, bt_export, kp_on, plabel_session, lab_exp_session, suite_hfs)
  )
